this is a production of Cornell  University  hi this is Frank Rossi for the Cornell  turfgrass video log and today we're  talking about the early-season outbreak  of dollar spot that we're experiencing  the persistent wet weather now with the  warm nighttime temperatures grass very  lush from that spring surge of growth  especially the higher cut turf we're not  seeing as much on putting greens but the  higher cut turf and approaches and  fairways key areas are experiencing a  lot more dollar spot than we would  normally see at this time so the best  thing to think about now is obviously to  get some of your early season  protections down maybe the pressure is  not so bad you might go with softer  chemicals like emerald civitas or  consider early season applications to  cure land there's a number of studies  that have shown those early season  applications can reduce overall pet  overall fungicide use for dollar spot  but also consider that you've got to  recover so make sure your nitrogen  fertility is adequate and that you're  able to get some recovery into these  areas and once you start thinking about  sort of getting on this right away  before you get epidemic levels a dollar  spot you should be able to work your way  right through it without any loss in  quality or performance this Frank Rossi  for the Cornell turfgrass video log this  has been a production of Cornell  University on the web at cornell.edu
 

